From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] loud_comp: report the latency of the FFT size in use (rebased on 1.2.37)

update_settings() reads the spectral processor's latency before it
passes the new FFT rank to it, so the dry-path delay and the reported
latency always describe the previous rank.  The processor starts at the
largest rank (16384 frames) and the dry delay line only holds 8192, so
after the first update the delay wraps to 7680 frames.  In FFT mode the
plugin then reports 7680 frames whatever the FFT size, while the audio
is delayed by exactly the FFT size, 1024 frames at the default of most
speaker graphs.  A later change of any setting fixes the value only for
the size before it.

Hosts that compensate latency (PipeWire's filter-chain publishes it as
the stream delay) mis-time the audio by the difference, and the dry
signal used when bypassing is out of step with the processed one.

Set the rank first and take the latency afterwards, and size the dry
delay line for the largest FFT, which needs 16384 frames.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
 modules/lsp-plugins-loud-comp/src/main/plug/loud_comp.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/modules/lsp-plugins-loud-comp/src/main/plug/loud_comp.cpp
+++ b/modules/lsp-plugins-loud-comp/src/main/plug/loud_comp.cpp
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@
                 c->sEqualizer.construct();
                 c->sClipInd.construct();
 
-                c->sDelay.init(1 << (meta::loud_comp_metadata::FFT_RANK_MAX - 1));
+                c->sDelay.init(1 << meta::loud_comp_metadata::FFT_RANK_MAX);
                 c->sProc.init(meta::loud_comp_metadata::FFT_RANK_MAX);
                 c->sProc.bind(process_callback, this, c);
                 c->sProc.set_phase(0.5f * i);
@@ -507,11 +507,12 @@
             for (size_t i=0; i<nChannels; ++i)
             {
                 channel_t * const c     = vChannels[i];
-                const size_t latency    = (nMode == meta::loud_comp_metadata::MODE_FFT) ? c->sProc.latency() : c->sEqualizer.get_latency();
 
                 c->sBypass.set_bypass(bypass);
                 c->sProc.set_rank(rank);
 
+                // Take the latency after the new rank is set, so it matches the processing
+                const size_t latency    = (nMode == meta::loud_comp_metadata::MODE_FFT) ? c->sProc.latency() : c->sEqualizer.get_latency();
                 c->sDelay.set_delay(latency);
                 if (rst_clip)
                     c->bHClip       = false;
